 "summary": "Singlepass(x86_64): wrong floating-point expansion for SSE path",
 "description": "### Summary\r\n\r\nWasmer's Singlepass compiler incorrectly generates SSE4.2 instructions for floating-point subtraction, division, comparisons, and float-to-integer conversions. Destination-register aliasing can reverse subtraction/division operands or overwrite conversion bounds, while incorrect comparison predicates cause gt/ge to return true for NaN operands.\r\n\r\n### Details\r\n\r\n\r\n### Proof of concept\r\n\r\n______________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n### Impact\r\n\r\nSPEC tests are not fulfilled.\r\n\r\n.",
